6d"},"seconds":13.819634199142456,"seed":1050160353603379086,"stop":"eos","text":"To find the hundreds digit in the product \\(5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 \\times 9 \\times 10\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the product**:\n    \\[\n    5 \\times 6 = 30\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    30 \\times 7 = 210\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    210 \\times 8 = 1680\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    1680 \\times 9 = 15120\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    15120 \\times 10 = 151200\n    \\]\n\n2. **Identify the hundreds digit**:\n   - The product is 151200.\n   - The hundreds digit is the third digit from the right.\n   - In 151200, the hundreds digit is 2.\n\nThus, the hundreds digit in the product is \\(\\boxed{2}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"To find the hundreds digit in the product \\(5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 \\times 9 \\times 10\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the product**:\n    \\[\n    5 \\times 6 = 30\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    30 \\times 7 = 210\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    210 \\times 8 = 1680\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    1680 \\times 9 = 15120\n    \\]\n    \\[\n    15120 \\times 10 = 151200\n    \\]\n\n2. **Identify the hundreds digit**:\n   - The product is 151200.\n   - The hundreds digit is the third digit from the right.\n   - In 151200, the hundreds digit is 2.\n\nThus, the hundreds digit in the product is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).","id":"number_theory:510"}
